he component with minimum size, until the number of left components does not equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"723E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/723/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"723E - One-Way Reform"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's solve this problem for each connected component separately."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At first we need to understand fact that in each connected component there are even number of vertices with odd degree. Let in the current connected component there are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices with odd degree and they have numbers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then we need to add in graph non-directional edges ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), ... ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"o"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). So in the current component now all vertices have even degree and there is exist Euler cycle, which we need to find and orientate all edges in the order of this cycle. It is easy to show that after that for all vertices which had even degree before we added the edges in-degree is equal to out-degree. In the other words, we show that the maximum number of vertices with equal in- and out-degrees in orientated graph equals to the number of vertices with even degree in non-orientated graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After we found Euler cycles for all connected components we need to print orientation of the edges and be careful and do not print edges which we added to the graph to connect vertices with odd degrees."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"723F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/723/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"723F - st-Spanning Tree"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At first lets delete vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the graph, find all connected components in the remaining graph and build for every component any spanning trees."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we need to add in spanning tree vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". At first let add edges from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to all components, which have no edges to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then let add edges from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to all components, which have no edges to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If after that the degree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" became more than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" or the degree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" became more than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" answer does not exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we have components which have edges and to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also currently we have two spanning trees which does not connect. Let's choose how to connect them — with vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", with vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text",